                                                              "summary":  "Damodaran examines the surge in US long-term treasury rates during 2026, with the 10-year reaching 4.75% and 20/30-year bonds topping 5%, against the backdrop of a new Fed chair, $40T in US debt, and geopolitical stress from the Iran war. He argues that rates are fundamentally driven by inflation expectations and real GDP growth ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â not Fed policy ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â and that the intrinsic 10-year rate is now nearly aligned with the observed market rate at approximately 5.4% vs. 4.75%. Despite rising rates, the S\u0026P 500 and Nasdaq posted strong gains through August 2026 because corporate earnings estimates were revised up 11%+ for both 2026 and 2027, cushioning the discount-rate headwind.",
